</div><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Chemistry_1e_(OpenSTAX)/12:_Kinetics/12.08:_Catalysis" class="mt-section" id="section_5"><span id="Summary"></span><h2 class="NoAuto editable">Summary</h2>

<p class="lt-chem-38264">Catalysts affect the rate of a chemical reaction by altering its mechanism to provide a lower activation energy. Catalysts can be homogenous (in the same phase as the reactants) or heterogeneous (a different phase than the reactants).</p>

